  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic Partnership VNG International Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description akvo:type="4" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening local governments to ensure an effective reconstruction effort in Syria</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="5" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Sustainable Development through Improved Local Governance Programme (SDLG) will mainly work with local councils on sub-district level (cities and towns) in Rural Damascus Governorate. 

Syria&#x2019;s governance structures are fragmented, local service delivery systems non-functional, and the social fabric deeply eroded. Conditions on the ground remain precarious: Basic services are absent, social cohesion is strained, and trust in governance is largely lost. Despite this, there is a clear and urgent need to begin investing in early recovery and local capacity, as a prerequisite for sustainable returns.

 To respond to this, the programme is structured around three pathways: It directly responds to the institutional, service delivery, and social cohesion gaps identified and provides an approach to recovery that balances immediate, visible improvements with longer-term governance strengthening.

By combining the development of strategic documents&#x2014;like local recovery and investment plans&#x2014;with practical implementation through mini-grants, the project delivers tangible results that are visible to citizens. This visibility helps to strengthen trust between local administrations and their communities.

&#x200b;</narrative>
  </description>
